 "pin_regs": {
  "enable": false,
  "clock": "stream_clk",
  "reason": "RTL registers every pin (KPREG=1, q9): stream inputs land in the wbk_q pin flops (rb_q/fb_q/re_q/fe_q/rt_q/rbase_q/wd_q/stk_c/q_s), stream outputs are flops (wb_ready/wa/wbw_*/fault); K outputs leave flops: w_k_v = vq_pin, w_k_wdata / w_k_addr = the registered ring heads hd (+ per-PC folded-address flop a6), cycle-identical to the KPREG=0 one-hot ring mux (lockstep bench, 0 added edges); w_k_wr_done lands in done_q (plain flop, all 16 bits); named exception: w_k_rdy (16 inputs) stays the ring's direct fire AND (registering it changes the K valid/ready protocol); a kit flop stage would add an unpriced edge and put a raw flop in front of the CDC FIFOs"
 },
