 "structural_change": "STEWARD-HBMd/PINREG q9 MAIN (10-23 coordinator tile review: 82% fill, 47% buf/inv, 4,593 pins w/o register on the 777.6 x 518.4 nd slot): KPREG=1 registered K ring heads (w_k_addr / w_k_wdata from flops, 0 added edges, lockstep-proven); outline sized from content at ~60-65% std fill and NOT squeezed; K ports split by bit range (pin_bit_groups): PCs 0-7 on N, PCs 8-15 on E, one pin segment per PC (its ring heads FIRM there by io_flop_at_pins); 32 SRAMs as 4 columns x 8 (one per stream_fifo_clk root, two abutted 4-stacks) at the W/centre, orient MY; std-cell bands N 240.648 um, E 196.776 um, S 59.4 um. RTL kq8 core otherwise = 1d2171e2e (source630 fanout repair + keep-without-dont_touch AND).",
 "slot_change_request": "d4g wbk_<q> x4: slot 777.6 x 518.4 -> 799.2 x 691.2 (MAIN; FB q9b 907.2 x 604.8); K ports of PCs 8-15 move from the N face to the E face (toward vmks_<q>2/3, right of / below wbk_<q>), PCs 0-7 stay on N (one segment per PC, PC 0 at the W end; E: PC 8 at the top); S face unchanged (DMA wd 2,312 + stream control toward hb_dbk_<q>); hbm_clk / hbm_rst_n at the N centre. Die notice: lanes/STEWARD-HBM.md NOTICE HBMd/CHAIN 10-23.",
 "job": {
  "owner": "STEWARD-HBMd/PINREG",
