 "reset_landing": {
  "enable": false,
  "reason": "RTL lands each reset at its face in 2 plain registered stages ON ITS OWN CLOCK (ot_hbm_svc_wb_kport_q srst_l0->srst_l1 on stream_clk, hrst_l0->hrst_l1 on hbm_clk); the kit landing supports one clock only and put hbm_rst_n on stream_clk (OT_MULTI_ROOT, gate 10-19 16:41)"
 },
 "safe_design_checklist": {
  "1_pins": "Every output leaves a flop (K heads hd/a6 + vq_pin, stream outputs); every data input lands in a pin flop (stream wd_q etc., K w_k_wr_done in done_q); resets land in 2 plain stages per own clock. Named exception: w_k_rdy x16 (direct ready of the K valid/ready handshake). Pins <= 3.9/um on every face.",
  "2_reach": "K ring heads FIRM at their PC segment (io_flop_at_pins); SRAM column -> crossbar -> PC crossing FIFO -> ring -> head stays inside the NE L-band, <= ~500 um at 833/1024 ps with the existing registered stages. RISK: the gate's 3_4 long-wire (wire*) buffer count is the evidence; > 15% of cells -> structural q10.",
  "3_fanout": "kq8 census-safe slicing unchanged (native max 32); KPREG adds per-slice kept rpob (ring+1 select: rpo alone would drive 33 loads), head D-mux selects <= 18 loads, w_k_rdy only selects the last head mux (fire).",
  "4_depth": "Head D = 3:1 AND-OR of ring entries (old output mux) + same-edge bypass mux + fire mux: the old pin-side mux moved before the flop, one 2:1 mux deeper on an hbm (1024 ps) flop->flop path.",
  "5_storage": "32 x 128x256 SRAM payload macros (4 columns x 8 aligned to the 4 stream_fifo_clk roots), reviewed <= 5-b ping-pong crossing FIFOs, 3-entry K rings + registered heads; no shift pipeline.",
  "6_floorplan": "799.2 x 691.2 sized from content (placed std 229.5k um2 of nd incl. long-wire buffers at ~60-65%), enlarged, never squeezed; SRAM block at the W/centre, logic bands N/E (K) and S (wd landing).",
  "7_clock": "Six clock ports as before (stream, four stream FIFO roots, hbm); hbm_clk at the N centre feeding the N/E K band; ~800-900 um span keeps the clock_span WARN -> measured pin-flop spread decides.",
  "8_schedule": "0 added edges on every path (KPREG lockstep: all outputs identical every stream and hbm edge); static schedule, K valid/ready at the HBM controller boundary unchanged; reset landing unchanged."
 },
